{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every screen that models its state with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" already knows exactly when it was opened and when it moves between Empty, Loading, Data, and Error. "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsService","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" turns those moments into "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"s and fans them out to as many "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsTracker","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"s as you register — one per analytics backend (Firebase, Mixpanel, Amplitude, your own logging endpoint, a debug console print, …)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"ScreenStates ships no backend-specific tracker implementations, so the core module stays dependency-free — but it does include ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/PrintScreenAnalyticsTracker"},{"text":" (logs every event to the console) and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/NoOpScreenAnalyticsTracker"},{"text":" (silently discards everything), so you don’t have to hand-roll a console logger just to confirm events fire at the right moments. For a real backend, write one small adapter, converting the event’s backend-agnostic ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/AnalyticsValue"},{"text":" parameters into that SDK’s own format:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["struct FirebaseScreenTracker: ScreenAnalyticsTracker {","    func track(_ event: ScreenAnalyticsEvent) {","        Analytics.logEvent(event.name, parameters: event.parameters.mapValues { value in","            switch value {","            case .string(let string): string","            case .int(let int): int","            case .double(let double): double","            case .bool(let bool): bool","            }","        })","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An adapter is also free to remap "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event.name"},{"type":"text","text":" to whatever vocabulary its backend expects — Firebase, for example, reserves a specific constant for screen views."}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Wiring-a-screen","type":"heading","text":"Wiring a screen"},{"code":["let analytics = ScreenAnalyticsService(trackers: [FirebaseScreenTracker(), PrintScreenAnalyticsTracker()])","","func onAppear(source: ScreenOpenSource<AppScreen>) {","    analytics.trackScreenOpened(\"Articles\", source: source.analyticsKind)","    analytics.observeStateChanges(of: store, screen: \"Articles\")","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackScreenOpened(_:source:)"},{"type":"text","text":" sends one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screen_opened"},{"text":" event. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"observeStateChanges(of:screen:)"},{"text":" uses the same ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withObservationTracking"},{"text":" mechanism ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateContainerView","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" uses to mirror a store, and sends a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screen_state_changed"},{"text":" event for every subsequent ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" transition — call it once, right where you create or first observe the store. When a transition lands on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".error"},{"text":", the event also carries the error’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"localizedDescription"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It also times how long the screen spends in ","type":"text"},{"code":".loading","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": the moment the state leaves ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".loading"},{"text":" for ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".empty"},{"text":", or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".error"},{"text":", it sends a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screen_load_duration"},{"text":" event (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent\/screenLoadDuration(screen:outcome:milliseconds:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":") with that outcome and the elapsed time in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"duration_ms"},{"text":" — useful for a “how long do loads actually take, and how often do they end in an error” dashboard without hand-rolling a stopwatch around every ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"load(_:)"},{"text":" call.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screen_state_changed"},{"text":" event landing on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".error"},{"text":" tells you a screen failed to load; it doesn’t tell you whether the user gave up or hit Retry. Call ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackRetryTapped(_:)"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent\/screenRetryTapped(screen:)"},{"text":") from the same ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onRetry"},{"text":" closure you pass to the Error placeholder, so that’s a distinct, countable event instead of indistinguishable from the screen’s initial ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".loading"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["ScreenStateView(store.state, onRetry: {","    analytics.trackRetryTapped(\"Articles\")","    Task { await store.load { try await api.fetchArticles() } }","}) { articles in","    ArticleList(articles)","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/loadNextPage(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" doesn’t move "},{"code":"state","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" off ","type":"text"},{"code":".data","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on either a success or a failure, so ","type":"text"},{"code":"observeStateChanges(of:screen:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has nothing to report for it — call ","type":"text"},{"code":"trackNextPageLoaded(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"trackNextPageFailed(_:errorDescription:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent\/screenNextPageLoaded(screen:)","type":"reference"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent\/screenNextPageFailed(screen:errorDescription:)","type":"reference"},{"text":") from the same place you call ","type":"text"},{"code":"loadNextPage(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", mirroring how "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackRetryTapped(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is called from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onRetry"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["func loadMore() async {","    await store.loadNextPage { try await api.fetchArticles(page: nextPage) }","    if let error = store.loadNextPageError {","        analytics.trackNextPageFailed(\"Articles\", errorDescription: error.localizedDescription)","    } else {","        analytics.trackNextPageLoaded(\"Articles\")","    }","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Both ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenOpenSource","type":"reference"},{"text":" expose an ","type":"text"},{"code":"analyticsKind","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" helper — a short, stable, payload-free name for the current case ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"loading\""},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"error\""},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"push\""},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"deep_link\""},{"text":", …) — so you can build custom ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"s yourself for anything the built-in factories don’t cover."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/trackinganalytics"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/TrackingAnalytics"},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Tracking Screen Analytics","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"role":"article"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[